{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1348698-help-me-with-ideas-for-the-far-northern-wyld","id":1348698,"title":"Help me with ideas for the far northern Wyld","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-15T11:59:32-08:00","id":1348698,"title":"Help me with ideas for the far northern Wyld","content":"Fimbulwinter is upon the world and Ragnarok is coming, as an angry Mela tries to freeze the world (maybe). My PCs are travelling from the Haslanti city of Crystal to the Elemental Pole of Air. There, they hope to either convince Mela to halt Fimbulwinter, or if necessary wrestle her into submission.<br /> <br /> So, the next session they'll be travelling across the Wasting Tundra towards the Border Marches of the North. Then into the Middle Marches, and eventually to Mela's Crystal Palace at the Elemental Pole of Air itself.<br /> <br /> &quot;Compass of Celestial Directions: The Wyld&quot; has a lot of stuff about the environment, but what I'd like is lots of ideas for weird monsters/animals/people that break the rules of nature and are appropriate for the North. Wyld mutants, behemoths, strange islands, weird Raksha who aren't just ice-elves. Also environmental oddities maybe, like the frozen fog and the weapon storms.<br /> <br /> The Compass had some ideas in: huge furry mutants who ride blue fanged horses, wolffolk, owlfolk, elkfolk, Raksha in ice-sleighs who steal children, the winged people of Sezakan, people made of ice or clouds or crystal, white hares with flaps of skin like flying squirrels, half-deer with two heads that split in two to watch for predators, giant ice wyrms, child-sized old men made of wind who can stop nearby wind and maintain the breath tunnels, a Raksha that's a great storm of feathers that rests as a series of concentric circles that bubbles at the centre, another that's a spreading stain served by bleeding icy dolls of moss and sticks.<br /> <br /> But I'd love to hear what other ideas you guys have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T13:12:07-08:00","id":1348719,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... Change things up by adding in some other elements.<br /> <br /> A Fire Elemental/Sun spirit/Fire themed Raksha/ Fire Manse that creates a hot valley full of jungle could be a nice change of pace. Or a burning man that travels the north in constant torment.<br /> <br /> A powerful wood elemental who has been trying to keep their forest from freezing (and possibly exploding) by increasingly desperate (and creepy) means.<br /> <br /> The god of Artificial Flight has a giant tower in the north somewhere.<br /> <br /> There are lots of Shadowlands in the north and various walking dead aren\u2019t necessarily common, but they certainly could be present. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d suggest looking through the Hundred Devils and Adversaries options and seeing if any of those sound useful <br /> <br /> You might go watch the trailer for the game Praey for the Gods, as it has some visuals you might find useful.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.praeyforthegods.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.praeyforthegods.com/cdn/shop/files/newwebsite2.jpg?v=1675978259\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.praeyforthegods.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Praey for the Gods </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.praeyforthegods.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.praeyforthegods.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> action-adventure survival game Boss climbing, Action-adventure survival game </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 11-15-2019, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T13:56:02-08:00","id":1348724,"title":"","content":"As always when creatures of the North come up, I'm going to push the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wendigo\" target=\"_blank\">wendigo</a>. It's a deliciously creepy piece of mythology. It could be a spirit or a Raksha, I think either interpretation works.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T03:18:05-08:00","id":1348822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1348698-help-me-with-ideas-for-the-far-northern-wyld?p=1348719#post1348719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... Change things up by adding in some other elements.<br /> <br /> A Fire Elemental/Sun spirit/Fire themed Raksha/ Fire Manse that creates a hot valley full of jungle could be a nice change of pace. Or a burning man that travels the north in constant torment.<br /> <br /> A powerful wood elemental who has been trying to keep their forest from freezing (and possibly exploding) by increasingly desperate (and creepy) means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not something I'd want to use too much, but a bit would add some variation. I like the Wood elemental one, it would be very fitting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The god of Artificial Flight has a giant tower in the north somewhere. </div> </div> </div>Vanileth. He has been mentioned in the game... I can't quite remember how.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are lots of Shadowlands in the north and various walking dead aren\u2019t necessarily common, but they certainly could be present. </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer to avoid undead as they can be kind of anywhere, and the other game we play features a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019d suggest looking through the Hundred Devils and Adversaries options and seeing if any of those sound useful </div> </div> </div>Cloud Person and Storm Serpents look good. As they're in an Airship, a Storm Serpent could actually reach them; some stuff they may just fly straight past. The Sky Titan doesn't fit per-se, but some other giant flying monster could use its stats.<br /> The Walkure (ghost-eating valkyrie monsters) I've already used a bit, could use them again.<br /> There's the Aughdeighe, the ice-horse. Probably just suitable for a random encounter, though as they can't fly it might be easy for the PCs to just ignore it. Still, it works as scenery.<br /> <br /> I'm also looking at the Zicnal and Mata-Yadh. Mata-Yadh has its aurora thing going on, that works for the North. I think I remember people saying its stats were a bit borked, but I don't remember why. Maybe just that it's built expecting you'll chop off limbs, but that's actually rubbish?<br /> <br /> <br /> You might go watch the trailer for the game Praey for the Gods, as it has some visuals you might find useful.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.praeyforthegods.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.praeyforthegods.com/</a>[/QUOTE]<br /> The fights on giant monsters worked (in the sky I mean). And gliding.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Has anyone got any idea for more society-esque things? Tribes, rather than monsters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T19:32:01-08:00","id":1348980,"title":"","content":"Thunderbird-worshippers are always fun. :-)<br /> <br /> Or you could always have a fae company that travels on a bank of freezing fog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T01:43:46-08:00","id":1349030,"title":"","content":"I like Dead of Winter/Game of Thrones.<br /> <br /> Ice Zombies.<br /> <br /> I know, you don't want Ice Zombies. But you can make them cool. It's the end of the world. There are mass dead. The Silver Prince works out of the North. Fey have found their ravaged slaves have died and have put their bodies to good use. Hungry Ghosts seek out sources of warmth, returning to ice frozen bodies in the day. You can have factions of undead vying with each other. Normal ghosts just trying to survive. Gives you that &quot;society&quot; edge -- side with the powerful Deathknight, accepting the North is lost but aiming to save Creation, bargaining with the fey, helping the spirits of the dead, putting down mindless zombies.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Throw in another vote for Thunderbird worshippers. Warlike Air Spirits and their drug crazed cultists driven insane by their own war paint. What's not to love? Has a real Mad Max vibe. Very societal.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> What's the Bull of the North up to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T01:44:38-08:00","id":1349031,"title":"","content":"Elementals and a human society that worships them... yeah, that seems suitable for the early stages of their journey. And as Thunderbirds can fly, it's one of the things they're less able to fly past on their airship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you could always have a fae company that travels on a bank of freezing fog.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in a company of friends... or a capitalist trading company? Because that's a bit different and I like it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Warlike Air Spirits and their drug crazed cultists driven insane by their own war paint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I like that.<br /> <br /> I wonder if anyone's done stats for Thunderbirds in 3rd ed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Silver Prince works out of the North. </div> </div> </div>He's in the far north-west though.<br /> They came from the North-East and are travelling right to, well, the North Pole.<br /> <br /> If I was to use a Deathlord, I'd use the Bishop of the Chalcedony Thurible, or the Lover Clad in the Raiment of Tears.<br /> Probably the Bishop, because his underlings (I'm not going to have the PCs fight him himself, Mela's bad enough for e2 Lunars) are more interesting than the Lover's, philosophically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hungry Ghosts seek out sources of warmth, returning to ice frozen bodies in the day. </div> </div> </div>That's good actually. They're undead, but specifically frozen-North-themed.<br /> <br /> Actually, while I'd like societies and interesting stuff going on with air-elementals, ice-men, etc, for ghosts I'd rather just have the occasional random encounter. You see, my previous game was about fighting the Walker in Darkness, with occasional clashes/manipulation with the Mask of Winter, and various Abyssals, navigating the Labyrinth, etc. The other game I play involves a lot of going into the Underworld, ghostly societies, a spectre cult, etc. So I don't want to lean into that.<br /> <br /> But the occasional undead random encounter is probably fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fey have found their ravaged slaves have died and have put their bodies to good use. </div> </div> </div>I think something death- or zombie-themed which is actually about the Wyld or Fae could work, good idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's the Bull of the North up to? </div> </div> </div>He's really too far away. Currently, they're in Crystal, which is over 2000 miles from most of the Bull's empire, with the entire Haslanti League in the way.<br /> Still... perhaps if he knows Mela is bringing about Fimbulwinter, he may send a small team of Exalts on their own stolen/hired airship to the North Pole as well.<br /> <br /> (Assuming he exists. One of my players thinks this game predates the Solars. The game was set in the far, far north-east, and the only one with a good Lore skill is from the furthest North-East. So rather isolated from the world. No-one knows what Realm Year it is, only their own local year systems. No PC has seen or heard of an operational Solar; it's just an ancient legend. There are rumours that have reached them that an army of demons is assailing the kingdoms of the South, the 666 Black Devil Kings; is this referring to Solars? Or actual demons? It's all very unclear, especially as rumours tend to conflate Lunars and other Demon champions. These demons were apparently summoned by Lakshi, ape-queen of the Anathema.<br /> Though you've reminded me, one PC comes from Gethemene, I should talk to him about the Bull of the North.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-17-2019, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}